# Core rules

Full manual: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Domain primer: [docs/context.md](docs/context.md).

**Context.** F1TENTH 1/10th-scale autonomous racing on ROS 2 Humble, developed in
Docker. Two racing stacks (classical raceline + pure-pursuit, and an end-to-end RL
policy) share perception/mapping/localization. The RL side follows GT Sophy:
QR-SAC ([training/qrsac/](training/qrsac/)) + a hand-designed observation
([libs/f1tenth_contract](libs/f1tenth_contract/)).

**Operating principles.** Verify before acting; prefer the conservative read; ask
over guessing; you own every line of the diff; keep diffs small; don't ship
speculatively; read before editing docs/config (targeted edits, not rewrites).

**Golden rules.**
- Keep it simple — no abstractions/layers/config/helpers until a second real caller needs them.
- No mocks — test real modules and real behavior; don't fake, stub, or skip a dependency to dodge it.
- Match existing patterns; edit an existing file rather than adding one.
- Respect [CODEOWNERS](CODEOWNERS); coordinate before touching vendored `src/vehicle/**`.

**Comment discipline.** Don't add comments/docstrings/type annotations to code you
didn't change. No ticket IDs, no historical narration ("previously…"), no
near-duplicate comments, no signature-restating docstrings, no unexplained jargon.

**Boundaries.**
- Always: build + test + lint before proposing; keep the diff in the module group in scope.
- Ask first: contract changes, vendored `src/vehicle/**`, new deps/packages, CI/deploy edits.
- Never: commit heavy artifacts; add company/internal names; skip tests/lint; self-merge.

**Where things go.** `src/` colcon packages · `libs/` shared contract · `training/`
pure Python (never colcon) · `deploy/` · `tools/` · `docs/`.

**Commands** (inside the dev container):
```bash
./tools/dev.sh up
./tools/build.sh [-t <group>]
./tools/test.sh [--packages-select <pkg>]
```
